   "text": "and phone if you want a specialist to confirm your exact price. How accurate is a moving cost calculator? A calculator gives you a realistic starting range, not a final quote. The biggest unknowns are how much you actually own, stairs or long walks at either home, and your exact date. An in-home or video survey turns the range into a firm price. How do movers price local and long-distance moves? Local moves are usually charged by the hour for a crew and truck. Long-distance moves are usually priced by the weight or volume of your belongings and the distance, with extras such as packing or stairs added on top. Does the estimate include packing? Only if you choose it. Packing, storage and car shipping are optional extras in the calculator, so you can see the price with and without them. When is the cheapest time to move? Demand peaks in summer, at weekends and at the start and end of each month, so mid-month weekdays outside May to September are usually the easiest dates to book at a good rate. Ready when you are Your estimate is one minute away, and you don't need to give us your email",
